+## Current activation (momentum transaction-cost sensitivity on the collected universe — R-001, agent 02, run 45639223642)
+
+Ran the bounded cost-sensitivity check (task R-001) that the LEARNING_STATE
+frontier flagged as the decision-relevant qualification of the admitted
+short-horizon momentum candidate: does the edge survive conservative
+transaction-cost stress under the repository's existing realistic cost model and
+a matched coin-flip null? Check `research/checks/momentum_cost_sensitivity.py`
+ran end-to-end (manifest 10/10 OK, preflight PASSED all data-quality and
+survivorship checks, leakage PASS on AMZN/JPM), and the independent verifier
+`research/checks/verify_momentum_cost_sensitivity.py` recomputed every reported
+value through a fresh `walk_forward` + `noise_benchmark` path (never calling
+`stress_segments`) and matched the artifact on all five gates.
+
+Predeclared cost grid (fixed a-priori, NOT tuned to results):
+- zero: no commission/slippage (reference).
+- realistic: the repository's existing realistic model
+  (commission_per_trade=2.0, commission_per_share=0.003, slippage_cents=2.0,
+  slippage_proportional=0.0005), matching examples/ma_crossover_real_data.py.
+- conservative: 2x the realistic variable costs
+  (commission_per_trade=4.0, commission_per_share=0.006, slippage_cents=4.0,
+  slippage_proportional=0.0010).
+
+Method: seed 42; dataset yf-ohlcv-universe-2009-to-2026-10-03; lookbacks {3,5,10};
+momentum (long previous N-day return, hold 1 day, daily rebalance) walk-forward
+per segment train=252d/test=84d/warmup=60d/overlap=60d, 4 contiguous volatility
+blocks, min 400 bars/segment; each segment's candidate median vs a coin-flip null
+run on the SAME segments with the SAME cost cfg (cost-matched null).
+
+Predeclared classification: a zero-cost positive edge = REGIME_STABLE with all
+segment medians > 0; an asset is ROBUST if >= 2 lookbacks have a zero-cost edge
+and all of those also survive conservative cost, FRAGILE if it has a zero-cost
+edge but none survive conservative, NO_EDGE if no zero-cost edge, PARTIAL if some
+but not all survive.
+
+Results:
+- Per-asset cost-robustness: ROBUST=5 (AAPL, GOOGL, AMZN, META, TSLA),
+  PARTIAL=1 (MSFT: zero-cost edges at lookbacks 3/5/10 but only 3/10 survive
+  conservative — the lookback-5 cell flips), FRAGILE=0, NO_EDGE=4 (NVDA, JPM,
+  JNJ, XOM — no zero-cost positive edge to erode).
+- 6/10 assets carry a zero-cost positive edge at >= 1 lookback; 5 of those 6 are
+  fully ROBUST and 1 is PARTIAL; none are FRAGILE.
+- Erosion magnitude (mean per-segment median, conservative minus zero, at the
+  reference lookback) is negligible for every edge asset (|erosion| <= 0.0004);
+  the only material number is NVDA (-0.0174), which has no zero-cost edge.
+- Overall classification: COST_ROBUST.
+
+Independent verification (five gates, all MATCH): Gate 1 fresh
+walk_forward + noise_benchmark recomputation of AMZN/JPM medians/nulls/segments/
+verdicts across all lookbacks x all cost levels; Gate 2 fresh conservative-cost
+medians/nulls/verdicts for all 10 assets x 3 lookbacks; Gate 3 zero-cost column
+cross-consistency against momentum_lookback_sweep_results.json (3-dp, all 30
+cells); Gate 4 per-asset and overall classification re-derived from the artifact
+medians/verdicts; Gate 5 determinism (AMZN conservative lookback-5 identical
+across two runs). Regression suite: 168 tests pass.
+
+Methodology observation (durable): the repository's constant-notional engine
+charges costs on actual traded notional, and per-bar notional rebalances are
+small relative to the large per-fold momentum edge, so realistic and
+conservative costs compress the per-fold medians by < 0.001 while the full-sample
+total return falls only ~1.5% (AMZN 5.54 -> 5.45 at conservative). A separate
+power check (diagnostic `research/checks/diag_momentum_cost3.py`, AMZN lookback 5)
